<!--
  MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1 Wave B — Wampa creature port, executing the owner's ruling
  (STARWARS_DONOR_SUNSET_1, question card 2026-09-02): "Wampa and Acklay: WIRE THEM
  IN — port both and give them real cast slots ... honoring the original adoption
  intent that never landed." Wampa was Tier C in the 2026-09-02 dependency census
  (no functional dependency — its own race/wildBiomes lists only cold biomes
  (BorealForest/Tundra/ColdBog/IceSheet), none of which Ash'karr has), so this is a
  DELIBERATE placement, not a natural fit: cast into ExtremeDesert at a low
  commonality (0.02) as a rare, dangerous nocturnal predator — the "night-side"
  half of the ruling, read as the harshest/coldest available biome on a desert
  world rather than a literal day/night spawn mechanic RimWorld does not have.

  Ported from mlie.starwarsanimalcollection's `Wampa` ThingDef/PawnKindDef pair,
  renamed under the RSW_ tier prefix. The donor's own ThingDef label was the sole
  bare "Wampa" (capitalized, unlike every other species' lowercase label) — kept as
  "wampa" here to match convention, not renamed to the defName.
  ⚠️ PRESERVED DONOR QUIRK, not a porting bug: both the left AND right claw tools
  link to RSW_SWLeftFingerClaw (the donor never wrote a right-hand tool entry) —
  cosmetically both attacks reference the same body-part group; left as the donor
  shipped it per this item's "stat-clone, not a balance pass" scope. Flag for a
  future code-review pass, same as the Bantha duplicate-horns fix.

  Custom body (RSW_Wampa, RSW_MlieWaveB_Bodies.xml), custom body-part-groups
  (RSW_SWLeftFingerClaw/RSW_SWRightFingerClaw, RSW_MlieWaveB_BodyParts.xml — only
  the left one is actually referenced, see above), leather/meat/trophy
  (RSW_Leather_Wampa, RSW_Reptomammal_Meat, RSW_WampaSkull,
  RSW_MlieWaveB_Resources.xml), sounds (RSW_Pawn_Wampa_*, already absorbed).
  `AttackTarget` is a VANILLA Odyssey TrainableDef (confirmed — not a donor def),
  kept MayRequire-gated as shipped.
-->
